{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unheavenly-callous-stag","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nCites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n`src/rebar/config.py::_resolve` (`:442-466`) and `resolve_with_sources` (`:774-800`) both run `_ordered_layers` + `Config.from_mapping(merge_sparse(...))`; user-then-project discovery is copied three times (`config.py:343-355`, `read_reserved_section:749-761`, `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py::_raw_toml_layers:86-102`). `src/rebar/_operation_config.py::compose_operation_snapshot` (`:203-227`) already delegates to `resolve_with_sources` (`:220`) and must keep doing so (ADR 0098 §1 `:83-96`; bindings `:230-311` untouched). `src/rebar/config.py` is exactly 800 lines on this basis — the hard cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`, enforced by the CI module-size gate with no allowlist — so this story must net-shrink it: the plan below lands the file at 778 lines, and the story lands at no more than that count.\n\n## Approach\n**`src/rebar/_config_sources.py`** — NEW after `_discover_project_config` (`:217`): `class RawLayer(NamedTuple): label, path, kind, raw` and generator `raw_layers(root=None) -> Iterator[RawLayer]` yielding `(\"user\", up, \"toml\", raw)` when `user_config_path().is_file()`, then `(\"project\", path, kind, raw)` from `_discover_project_config`. Lazy: each file parses as yielded, so a tolerant caller keeps earlier layers on a `ConfigError`.\n\n**`src/rebar/config.py`** —\n- KEEP `LAYER_ORDER`, `_env_signature` (minus `:382-385`, deleted by the alias story), `_cli_signature`, `_file_token`, `_config_probe_paths`, `set_cli_overrides`, `parse_cli_overrides`, `reset_config_cache`, `_RESULT_CACHE`.\n- REWIRE `_ordered_layers` (`:330-359`, name/signature kept — `tests/unit/test_config_perf.py:195-223` monkeypatches it as the walk seam): the body iterates `raw_layers(root)`, coerces each with `source=str(rl.path)`, records `proj=(rl.path, rl.kind)` for the project layer, then appends env/cli as today.\n- DELETE `_resolve` (`:442-466`). NEW `class _Resolution(NamedTuple): config, sources, project, validation` and `_compose(root, cli_overrides) -> _Resolution`: one `_ordered_layers` call (module-global lookup), `Config.from_mapping(merge_sparse(...))`, the provenance loop moved from `:791-799` into helper `_winning_label(layers, sect, key)`, the validation tokens moved from `:451-466` into `_validation_tokens(root, proj)`.\n- KEEP `load_config` (`:469-519`); `:517-519` becomes `res = _compose(root, effective_cli); _RESULT_CACHE[key] = (res.config, res.validation); return res.config`.\n- KEEP the `resolve_with_sources` signature; body becomes `res = _compose(root, effective_cli); return res.config, res.sources, res.project` (uncached, as today).\n- REWIRE `read_reserved_section` (`:739-762`): `for rl in raw_layers(root): sub = rl.raw.get(name); if isinstance(sub, dict): merged.update(sub)` (shallow per-key, project over user — pinned by `tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py:221-250`).\n- Re-export `RawLayer`, `raw_layers` in the `_config_sources` import block (`:43-87`).\n\n**`src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`** — REWIRE `_raw_toml_layers` (`:86-102`): iterate `_config.raw_layers(root)` appending `(str(rl.path), rl.raw)`; `except ConfigError: return layers` preserved (the generator keeps the partial list). KEEP `_merge_raw_tables`, `_typed_config_errors` (minus `:142-146`, deleted by the alias story), `_validate`, `_resolved` (`:39-53` — provenance labels unchanged: `cli > env > project > user > default`).\n\n**`src/rebar/_operation_config.py`** — unchanged.\n\n**Docs** — `docs/reuse-surface.md:587-592`: add the `raw_layers` sentence. `docs/config.md:88-99` unchanged (behaviour identical).\n\n**Tests** — `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`: add the malformed-project partial-layer test (the Edge case in Testing).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/config.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`, `docs/reuse-surface.md:587-592`, `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`. Out of scope: `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` (`compose_operation_snapshot:203-227` keeps delegating to `resolve_with_sources`; bindings `:230-311` untouched), `docs/config.md:88-99`, the alias-story deletions (`config.py:382-385`, `show_config.py:142-146`) which land before this story, and any change to precedence order, provenance labels, cache keys, and the `resolve_with_sources` and `_ordered_layers` signatures.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_config_show.py tests/unit/test_config_perf.py tests/unit/test_config_cli_overrides.py tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_mapping_config.py tests/unit/test_config_llm.py -q`.\n- `rebar -c sync.push=off config` shows `sync.push = off [cli]`; `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=async rebar config --output json | jq .sources.sync.push` → `\"env\"`; with `[sync] push='always'` in `rebar.toml` and no env → `\"project\"`.\n- Edge: malformed `rebar.toml` + `~/.config/rebar/config.toml` carrying `[verify] require_verdict_for_close=true` → `rebar config validate` still prints the user-file ERROR (partial-layer tolerance preserved); `rebar config` exits 1 with `rebar config: could not read config …`. This case is added to `tests/unit/test_config_show.py`.\n- `wc -l src/rebar/config.py` ≤ 778; `ruff check --select C901 src/rebar/config.py src/rebar/_config_sources.py src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (`new=0 increased=0`); `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 `git grep -n '_discover_project_config\\|user_config_path().is_file' -- src/rebar/config.py src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py` shows only `_config_probe_paths`/`_validation_tokens` (no discovery copy) (verified by the grep).\n- [ ] AC2 `tests/unit/test_config_show.py:157-164` (`resolve_with_sources` ≡ `load_config`) and `tests/unit/test_config_perf.py:185-227` green (verified by `pytest`).\n- [ ] AC3 `tests/unit/test_operation_snapshot.py` green unchanged (ADR 0098 bindings preserved) (verified by `pytest`).\n- [ ] AC4 `wc -l src/rebar/config.py` reports at most 778 lines (the planned count; the 800 hard cap is met with margin) and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`; `make verify` green.","id":"e123-cf0f-f3f8-496c","parent_id":"e12f-a994-29d3-4f72","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Collapse `config.py` to one precedence composer and one file-discovery generator"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807590424203228,"uuid":"b737a100-7c03-4635-ba58-ba71c525eab6"}